docs/chiri/adr/0007-suggestion-lifecycle.md:15:- **Active Suggestion:** shows the Accept / Reject / Refine toolbar. Its Rationale shows on hover, and when the text cursor is inside it (keyboard users can't hover). Other Suggestions show only the inline diff.
docs/chiri/adr/0007-suggestion-lifecycle.md:16:- **Keys, with the cursor inside a Suggestion:** `Cmd/Ctrl+Enter` Accepts, `Esc` Rejects. Accept is a normal edit, so `Cmd+Z` undoes it. Reject is not undoable in v1. A Review pass also offers Accept all and Reject all.
docs/chiri/adr/0007-suggestion-lifecycle.md:21:  - Failed call (network, `402` out of credit, `429`): the Suggestion becomes an error card with Retry. `402` gets its own message.
docs/chiri/adr/0007-suggestion-lifecycle.md:23:  - Timeout: 30 s.
docs/chiri/adr/0007-suggestion-lifecycle.md:28:- An accidental `Esc` loses a Suggestion. An undoable Reject is in the backlog.
